   "definition_quote": "We study the problem of minimizing the number of samples $\\budget$ required to construct an estimator $\\bxh$ of $\\bx$ such that $|f(\\bx)-f(\\bxh)|\\le \\epsilon$ with probability at least $1-\\delta$. The function $f:\\R^n\\mapsto\\R$ is known, and is differentiable with $L$-Lipschitz gradients... at each time step $t\\in \\N$ we select $i\\in [n]$ and obtain $\\mu_i+Z_{i,t}$, where $\\{Z_{i,t}\\}$ are independent standard normals."
